  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Always give four unique sentence choices and exactly one right future form.",
      "The right choice is will plus the base verb. Be-verb stems become will be.",
      "Never offer going to, gonna, or shall. Those can look like future too.",
      "Wrong choices are the unchanged stem, a present form, a past form, or a broken future.",
      "Broken future means will plus a past form, will plus -ing, or will plus has, are, were, am, or is.",
      "Keep the same subject, names, and kid-world details in every choice. Do not swap in a new verb.",
      "Stems must be clearly present or past. Do not put will, tonight, or tomorrow in a stem.",
      "Tier 3 must include one near-miss such as will has, will are, will were, or will plus the old past form."
    ]
  },
